    "plain": "This policy promises 60,000 extra specialist school places and 15 new free schools for children with SEND, which would help a system already under severe strain \u2014 but the places will take many years to materialise, and there is no committed high-needs funding plan to go with them.",
    "biggest_unknown": "Whether the promised capital investment translates into operational places without squeezing mainstream school budgets, given the OBR's projected \u00a36 billion funding gap by 2028-29.",
